{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]She was a level headed dancer on the [C]road to alcohol.
And [D]I was just a soldier on my way to [G]Montreal.
Well she [G]pressed her chest against me,
About the [C]time the jukebox broke.
Yeah, she [D]gave me a peck on the back of the neck,
And [D]these are the words she [G]spoke.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Blow up your [G]TV, Throw away your paper.
Go to the [D]country, Build you a [G]home.
Plant a little [G]garden.  Eat a lotta peaches.
Try and find [D]Jesus,  on your [G]own.[D][G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Well, I sat there at the table, and I acted real naive.
For I knew that topless lady, had something up her sleeve.
Well, she danced around the bar room, and she did the hoochy-coo.
Yeah she sang her song all night long, tellin' me what to do.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Well, I was young and hungry, and about to leave that place.
When just as I was leavin', well she looked me in the face.
I said "You must know the answer".  She said "No but I'll give it a try".
And to this very day, we've been livin' our way.
And here is the reason why.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
We blew up our [G]T.V.  Threw away our paper.
Went to the [D]country, built us a [G]home.
Had a lot of [G]children, fed 'em on peaches.
They all found [D]Jesus, on their [G]own.[C][G]
{end_of_verse}
